+# Homepage components
+
+Load `homepage.js` once with a module script. It registers three autonomous
+custom elements without dependencies or build tooling:
+
+| Element | Named slots | Shadow parts |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `coffee-card` | `title`, `description`, `action` | `card` |
+| `coffee-hero` | `title`, `description`, `action` | `hero` |
+| `grind-navigation` | `brand`, `links` | `navigation`, `toggle`, `links` |
+
+Supply native headings, paragraphs, and anchors directly in the slots. Choose
+heading levels appropriate to the surrounding document and give repeated detail
+links descriptive accessible names. Content and destinations remain editable in
+HTML and readable even when JavaScript is unavailable.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="title">Cold Brew</h3>
+  <p slot="description">Steeped for 18 hours for maximum smoothness.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/cold-brew"
+     aria-label="View details for Cold Brew">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+Each instance clones a shared template into its own open shadow root. Component
+styles use inherited `--primary`, `--text`, and `--accent` properties with fallback
+values; cards also accept `--card-background`, and heroes accept `--hero-image`
+(a CSS image value such as `url(...)`). Use the documented parts for additional
+styling. Slotted content remains consumer-owned; page selectors can override its
+styles. Layout of the component hosts belongs to the page.
+
+Navigation accepts any number of direct anchors in its `links` slot. Add
+`data-outlined` to highlight an anchor. At widths up to 48rem, a native button
+toggles the links and synchronizes `aria-expanded` and visibility. Escape closes
+the menu and returns focus to the button; link activation closes it as well.
+Breakpoint changes keep focus on visible controls. Event listeners are removed
+on disconnect and reinstated on reconnect, independently for each instance.
+The button and its `aria-controls` target live in the same shadow root, so IDs
+can safely repeat across component instances.
+
+The existing site routes and stock hero photo are preserved. This project has no
+build script; it can continue to be served as static files.
